.Dd @MDOCDATE@
.Dt TROUPE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm troupe
.Nd clown-owned messaging surface over the job-wakeup channel
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm send
.Fl -target Ar session-key | group | '*'
.Brq Fl -message Ar text | Fl -subject Ar subject Op Fl -body Ar body
.Op Fl -from Ar sender-key
.Op Fl -source Ar source
.Op Fl -resource Ar uri
.Nm
.Cm read
.Op Fl -peek
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Cm message
.Fl -target Ar session-key | '*'
.Op Fl -from Ar sender-key
.Op Fl -source Ar source
.Fl -message Ar body
.Op Fl -result-ref Ar ref
.Op Fl -resource Ar uri
.Nm
.Cm mcp
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is clown's messaging surface (RFC-0015): the standalone binary that carries
cross-session chat (RFC-0013 section 3) and the standalone waking message,
built on the job-wakeup channel (see
.Xr ringmaster 1 ) .
Its current transport is the on-disk job channel; the CLI is specified
transport-abstract so a future XMPP backend can replace the journal without
changing the surface.
A chat message is a
.Em chat
record \(em a waking, non-terminal type distinct from
.Em message \(em
whose one-line subject is the wake notification and whose full body is stored in
the message's output spool, so a long body never truncates the wake line.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nm Cm send
Send a chat message.
.Fl -target
is a session key (a single clown, addressed by its per-instance key), a
group-id
.Pq Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID
label (fans out to every clown under that group), or
.Ql *
for broadcast.
The message is given one of two ways.
.Fl -message
is the preferred form: a single string in git-commit format \(em a concise
one-line summary, a blank line, then the body \(em which
.Nm
splits into the wake subject (the first line) and the body recovered by
.Nm Cm read
(the remainder).
A body that follows the summary without an intervening blank line is rejected.
Alternatively, give the two parts explicitly with
.Fl -subject
(the one-line wake notification) and the optional
.Fl -body .
Exactly one of
.Fl -message
or
.Fl -subject
is required, and they are mutually exclusive.
.Fl -from
defaults to this session's key.
.Fl -resource
attaches a resource reference (a
.Li madder://blobs/ Ns Ar digest
URI or any fetchable URI); repeat it to attach several (clown#112).
clown carries the reference only \(em the blob store is external (madder); the
reader fetches the URI itself.
Prints the generated job id.
.It Nm Cm read
Read chat messages addressed to this session \(em its own (direct), group, and
broadcast channels \(em newer than the read cursor, oldest first, each body
recovered from its spool.
The read advances a per-reader cursor distinct from the wake monitor's, so a
wake never consumes a read and a read never consumes a wake.
Unlike the wake monitor, which suppresses the sender's own messages, it shows
this session's own sends that land on a channel it reads \(em its group,
broadcast, and self-directed sends (conversation history).
A direct send to another session is delivered to that session's channel, not
this one, so it does not appear in your own read; the recipient reads it from
their channel.
Any resource references carried by a message
.Pq Fl -resource No on send
are listed beneath it.
.Fl -peek
reads without advancing the cursor.
.Fl -json
emits one JSON object per message
.Pq Li {job,from,source,scope,subject,body,resources,ts} .
.It Nm Cm list
List the live chat recipients, grouped by their group decoration (the
.Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID
value).
Each entry shows the recipient's per-instance key and its
.Ev CLOWN_GROUP_DESCRIPTION .
.Fl -json
emits one JSON presence record per line.
.It Nm Cm message Fl -target Ar session-key | '*' Oo Fl -from Ar sender-key Oc Oo Fl -source Ar source Oc Fl -message Ar body Oo Fl -result-ref Ar ref Oc Oo Fl -resource Ar uri Oc
Emit a standalone single-record waking
.Li message
job (promoted from the former
.Li clown job message ,
RFC-0015 section 3): a self-contained job whose only record
.Pq Li seq No 0 , job id Li msg- Ns Ar 8-hex
is the non-terminal waking
.Li message
event \(em no
.Li started ,
no terminal record.
Prints the job id and exits
.Li 0 .
.Fl -target
and
.Fl -message
are required; a missing
.Fl -target
or a missing or empty
.Fl -message
is a usage error
.Pq exit Li 2 .
.Fl -target Ar '*'
addresses the reserved broadcast channel.
This is a messaging operation by concept \(em the matching
.Li job_message
MCP tool belongs to the troupe surface (clown#144) \(em so it lives here rather
than on
.Xr ringmaster 1 .
When the facility is disabled via
.Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_JOB_WAKEUP ,
.Cm message
is a no-op that still exits
.Li 0 .
.It Nm Cm mcp
Serve the troupe tool surface of the job-platform MCP server (RFC-0011): a
stdio JSON-RPC server exposing the messaging tools
.Li chat_send ,
.Li chat_read ,
.Li chat_list ,
and the standalone
.Li job_message ,
surfaced to the agent as
.Li plugin:clown-builtin-jobs:troupe .
Normally spawned by
.Nm clown
as a synthesized
.Xr clown-json 5
stdioServers entry, not run by hand; see
.Xr ringmaster 1
.Cm mcp
for the job-control half.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CLOWN_SESSION_ID
The reader's per-instance key; its channel is the direct-message target (see
.Xr ringmaster 1 ) .
.It Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID
The group decoration; chat read also services the group channel
.Pq Li ChannelID Ns Pq Ev CLOWN_GROUP_ID .
.It Ev CLOWN_DISABLE_JOB_WAKEUP
When set to
.Li 1 ,
disables the facility;
.Cm message
becomes a no-op exiting
.Li 0 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clown 1 ,
.Xr ringmaster 1 ,
.Xr clown-json 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC-0015 (ringmaster and troupe platform binaries), RFC-0013 (clownfile,
per-instance identity, and clown-owned chat), and RFC-0009 (job-wakeup
channel).
.Sh AUTHORS
.An "amarbel, LLC"
